Fight engine 8.0.0, params 8.0.0-selfcal-pre2024; 1229 fighters; N = 8000

=== API and determinism ===
PASS  API surface  (VERSION 8.0.0)
PASS  no learned model loaded by default: matchup = base tables
PASS  engine source has no Math.random
PASS  engine runs with Math.random disabled
PASS  same seed, same fight
PASS  same seed, same summary
PASS  trace on/off gives the same fight (400 seeds)
PASS  trace parity holds over a shared rng stream
PASS  worker-style concatenation (self.FightParams + self.MLRates + self.FightEngine) reproduces Node results
PASS  worker-style loadMLRates reproduces Node's learned-rate matchup

=== Engine v4: learned stat-line rates (loadMLRates / opts.ml) ===
PASS  matchup without a model equals matchupBase
PASS  with a model loaded matchup applies the learned rates  (distance attempt ratio Volk 0.86, Gaethje 0.93)
PASS  opts.ml === false keeps the base tables
PASS  params.mlWeight 0 keeps the base tables
PASS  opts.ml = { pred } reproduces the loaded model's tables  (max rel diff dRate 0.0e+0)
PASS  ML: same seed, same fight
PASS  ML: matchup is deterministic (same tables twice)
PASS  ML: trace on/off gives the same fight (150 seeds)
PASS  ML: predict(A, B) and predict(B, A) swap exactly
PASS  ML: swapping corners mirrors the learned tables  (max rel diff 2.2e-16)
PASS  ML: swapping corners swaps the probabilities  (Volk 68.1% as A vs 68.1% as B; base tables 61.2%)
PASS  ML: a fighter vs his clone wins about 50%  (51.5% of non-draws)
PASS  ML: Volk chin knob 1.6 raises Gaethje's KO/TKO share  (11.9% -> 16.4%)
PASS  ML: league-average pair keeps the league level (finish rate within 4 pts, sig landed within 8%)  (finish 52.5% -> 48.9%, sig landed 42.0 -> 43.3)

=== Engine v4: train-only priors (hidden-data protocol) ===
PASS  data/derived/priors_dev.json exists and stops before 2024-01-01
PASS  train-only priors hold fewer fights than the production priors  (Lightweight 406 vs 608)
PASS  params are labelled as self-calibrated on the train-only priors  (8.0.0-selfcal-pre2024)

=== Engine v4: judges (EM weights, shared + fight-level noise, 10-8 rule) ===
PASS  judge weights are the EM fit
PASS  an even round is a coin flip  (P(A) 50.2%)
PASS  judging is corner-symmetric (mirrored differentials mirror the round)  (86.5% vs 86.6%)
PASS  more output wins more rounds  (P(A) 86.5% for +6 head, +2 body, +1 leg, +1 TD, +30 s control)
PASS  10-8s come with lopsided rounds, rarely with even ones  (lopsided 62.4%, even 0.00%)
PASS  a lone knockdown edge usually wins the round  (P(KD scorer) 91.2%)
PASS  non-unanimous share of even-looking rounds near the data (MMA Decisions |EM| < 0.5: 43%)  (42.3%)
PASS  decision split and 10-8 share in a sane band  (UD 80.8%, SD 18.8%, 10-8 3.36% per judge-round)

=== Trace format ===
PASS  event kinds are from the spec table (+ esc)  (miss hit clinch break tdx td esc up pass)
PASS  events carry t, k, w, s, snapshots; strikes carry tg and loc; subs carry name; fin carries how
PASS  event times are ordered within each round
PASS  all spec kinds occur over 300 traced fights  (miss hit clinch tdx break td up kd fin hurt pass esc subx recover reset sweep sub)
  sample event: {"t":38.43,"k":"hit","w":"B","s":0,"dA":0,"dB":0,"gA":0.8,"gB":0,"sA":0.977,"sB":0.951,"tg":2,"loc":"dist"}
  result: A UD | Unanimous Decision (48-47, 48-47, 49-46) | round 5 at 300.0 s | cards [[48,47],[48,47],[49,46]]

=== Symmetry and clones ===
PASS  swapping corners swaps the probabilities  (Volk 61.6% as A vs 60.8% as B; 4 se = 3.1)
PASS  swapping corners mirrors the 7 outcome bins  (max bin diff 1.2 pts)
PASS  alexander-volkanovski vs his clone wins about 50%  (50.9% of non-draws, 4 se = 2.2)
PASS  justin-gaethje vs his clone wins about 50%  (50.0% of non-draws, 4 se = 2.2)
PASS  league-average vs league-average wins about 50%  (50.0%)

=== Knob directions (Volk = A, Gaethje = B) ===
PASS  chin knob up on A -> more KO losses for A  (17.6 -> 24.7)
PASS  chin knob down on B -> fewer KO losses for B  (14.3 -> 10.3)
PASS  power knob up on A -> more KO wins for A  (14.3 -> 22.0)
PASS  output knob up on A -> more attempts by A  (209.3 -> 263.6)
PASS  accuracy knob up on A -> higher accuracy for A  (57.6 -> 66.4)
PASS  cardio knob up on A (tires faster) -> lower win share for A  (60.9 -> 53.3)
PASS  takedown-attempt knob up on A -> more TD attempts and control for A  (TD att 3.38 -> 8.54, ctrl 99 -> 185 s)
PASS  takedown-defense knob up on B -> lower TD success for A  (28.0 -> 16.9)
PASS  leg-kick share knob on B -> more leg kicks by B  (8.8% -> 36.4% of attempts)
PASS  submission knob up on A -> more submission wins for A  (3.9 -> 9.8)
PASS  judges.power up -> decisions shift toward the harder hitter  (Gaethje's share of decisions 28.8 -> 53.5 (damage/head 0.56 vs 0.85))

